// The reduct the checker applies, written out (#2030). In the explicit form,
// a monoid standing where a semigroup is asked is written as the reduct's
// call, `Monoid.Semigroup(endoMonoid)`; the sugared form leaves that call to
// the checker. The formatter writes the call where the checker applies the
// reduct and keeps it here, and the run reads the same application in both
// forms.

// The semigroup, the monoid, and the endomorphism monoid.
import "./monoid.gandr";
// The endomorphism monoid and a reader of a semigroup.
import "./reduct.gandr";

/// The monoid where a semigroup is asked, with the reduct the checker applies
/// written out.
@[ runs("0"), form(explicit) ]
def asSemigroupWritten() -> -F Integer {
  become multiplies(Monoid.Semigroup(endoMonoid))
}
